        "mission_intent": "Team, we need to revamp how our SOC handles log analysis reporting to better align with NIST SP 800-92 guidance. Specifically, I want us to implement a dual-report structure for our SIEM output: a high-priority report that surfaces entries identified as known malicious or matching our established threat signatures, and a secondary report that captures entries not yet fully categorized or understood against our current logging baseline. The high-priority report should drive automated alerting to on-call analysts and trigger pre-defined response playbooks where applicable, including automated reconfiguration of perimeter security controls when confidence is high. The secondary report needs to be reviewed regularly so we can continuously expand and refine our logging baseline over time\u2014if we neglect that second report, we'll stagnate on what we can detect. I'd like the automated filtering rules configured so that the volume of entries surfaced for manual review in the primary report is manageable for the analyst team on each shift. Please coordinate with the infrastructure team to ensure our log sources across network devices, OS-level logs, and application logs are all feeding into this framework. Get me an implementation plan by end of next week.",
